-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart for the completed supersingular stalk
-- statement:
--   Fix the following data.
--
--   *Arithmetic data.* A prime $q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`).
--
--   *Coefficient field and roots of unity.* A field $L$ of characteristic $0$, an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, an element $\xi \in L$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, with $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$ (`hζξ`), and the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfies $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   *Level subgroup and function field.* A subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ equal (by `hH₁`) to the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. An intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ (Laurent series over $L$) equal (by `hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   *Base ring.* A discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its field of fractions, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$; an element $j \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the $q$-expansion $\mathsf q^{-1} + \dots$ of the modular invariant $j$), with $j \neq 0$; and a uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$, so that the maximal ideal of $A$ is $(\varpi)$ (`hϖ`).
--
--   *The constant $t$.* An element $t \in A$ for which there is a unit $w \in A$ with $t^{\,q-1} = q\,w$ (`ht`).
--
--   *The point.* Write $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the scheme obtained by gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$ along the middle chart. Fix a point $z$ of $X$, and let $\varpi z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ through the structure morphism $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ (`hϖz`); it is assumed that $\varpi z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`), so $z$ lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Fix a point $y$ of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) mapping to $z$ (`hy`).
--
--   *Supersingularity at $y$.* The hypothesis `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime ideal of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist: a ring $W$ which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring, and complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal; a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ such that the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\sigma(\varpi)$; power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and
--   $$f - \big(X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1\big) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   where $X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1$ is [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18); and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma t)\,v - f\,u\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}$ denotes the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ at its maximal ideal, subject to the following seven conditions. Write $\mathrm{toC} : \mathcal{O}_{X,z} \to \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}$ for the canonical map, $\mathrm{mkS} : W[[X_0,X_1]] \to S$ for the quotient map, and $\mathrm{germY} :$ `chartAlgFin A K j` $\to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the canonical map coming from the affine chart at the point $y$ above $z$.
--
--   (1) For every $a \in A$, the image under $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ of the germ at $z$ of $a$ (taken through the structure morphism $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$) equals $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma a))$.
--
--   (2) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is: for every weight $k$, every pair $f_0, g_0$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ such that the Laurent series attached to $p_g$ is nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the quotient of the series of $p_f$ by that of $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g_0 \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f_0 \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}\delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q\\ q\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ — such $\tau$ maps `chartAlgFin A K j` into itself.
--
--   (3) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, every $\tau$ as in (2) for $\gamma^{-1}$, and every proof `hpres` that $\tau$ preserves `chartAlgFin A K j`, the restriction of $\tau$ to `chartAlgFin A K j` satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y$ (the prime ideal of $y$) for all $a$ in that algebra.
--
--   (4) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ as in (2) for $\gamma^{-1}$, every proof `hpres` that $\tau$ preserves `chartAlgFin A K j`, and under the assumption that the restricted $\tau$ satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for all $a$ in that algebra, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{M}_2(W)$ such that: (a) $\theta \circ e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} = e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} \circ \tau$ on `chartAlgFin A K j`; (b) $\theta$ fixes $\mathrm{mkS}(C w)$ for every $w \in W$; (c) for each index $j' \in \{0,1\}$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_{j'})) - \mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_{i} C(M_{ij'})X_i\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$; (d) $c^{\,q+1} - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$; (e) $M_{ij'} - c\,\gamma_{ij'}$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$ for all $i, j'$ (the entries of $\gamma$ being read in $W$); (f) if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$; (g) if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$, then $c - 1$ does not lie in the maximal ideal of $W$.
--
--   (5) For all integers $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ such that, for each $i$, at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$ is outside $P_i$, the element $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$ lies in $P_i$, and $P_i$ contains an element of the form $\mathrm{mkS}\big(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h\big)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and such that $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$: the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct.
--
--   (6) For every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ with at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$ outside $P$, with $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi)) \in P$, and containing an element of the form $\mathrm{mkS}\big(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h\big)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$: for all $a$ in `chartAlgFin A K j`, the element $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $L((\mathsf q))$, is the image of an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   (7) A moduli–Hasse clause: there exist a proof that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the series obtained from the $q$-expansion of $j$ by the substitution $\mathsf q \mapsto \mathsf q^{q}$ — lies in $K$, a proof that the resulting element of $K$ lies in `chartAlgFin A K j`, an element $a_0 \in A$ with that element minus the image of $a_0$ lying in the prime ideal of $y$, a natural number $e_0 \ge 1$ and a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that: for all $a, b \in W$ with at least one of $a, b$ outside the maximal ideal of $W$ and with $a^{q}b - ab^{q}$ in the maximal ideal of $W$, the element
--   $$\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \big(\text{coefficient of } X_0^{\,i}X_1^{\,e_0-i} \text{ in } h\big)\,a^{i}b^{\,e_0-i}$$
--   is a unit of $W$; and $e\big(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\text{that element} - a_0))\big) = \mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   This is the local analysis of the integral two-chart model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: the completed stalk is identified with a Drinfeld-type chart $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(tv - fu)$ with $f$ congruent to $X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1$ to order $q+2$, together with the induced action of the level automorphisms, the separation of the branches through the point, and a Hasse-invariant normalisation of the $j(\mathsf q^{q})$ parameter. It is the variant of that analysis adapted to the auxiliary guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and to small $q$, and it feeds the construction of supersingular affine charts and the computation of the semilinear inertia action on the Drinfeld chart.
